{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "19 feels like a natural choice because expressive singing and melodic ballads connect with the strong vocal performances I have been choosing.",
    "God's Problem Child fits my interest in warm, reflective country songs, while Abbey Road appeals through tuneful songs and vocal harmonies."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger, Appetite For Destruction and Lateralus feel too heavy and intense when I want relaxing melodies and expressive vocals.",
    "Led Zeppelin, A Farewell to Kings and By the Way emphasize rock styles I am not seeking now; Revelator gives me too little information to feel confident choosing it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat my interest in some familiar songs as a broad interest in well-known rock albums.",
    "My listening across several musical styles seems to have been taken as interest in a much wider range of energy and intensity than I currently want."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice explicitly emphasizes relaxing classical music, which makes a calm mood especially relevant to what I would choose next.",
    "My repeated choices of vocal albums and television music suggest that expressive singing, orchestral arrangements and accessible melodies matter more to me than simply sharing a broad musical style."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my taste for melodic singing but miss how much a relaxing mood and warm vocal performances matter to me right now."
}"}
